Adapted by Corepass
===================

The upstream MCP servers authenticate with a bearer token the user pastes
(`Authorization: Bearer ${ZOOM_*_MCP_ACCESS_TOKEN}`): Claude Code users run
Zoom's OAuth themselves and export the token, which expires hourly. In Remy
the servers sign in through Remy's own Zoom app instead, so:

- `.mcp.json`: the same seven endpoints, without the `Authorization` headers.
  Remy matches each URL to its Zoom provider and signs in through it.
- `CONNECTORS.md` "Authentication", the install paragraph of `README.md`, and
  the "Claude Code" auth rule in `skills/setup-zoom-mcp/SKILL.md` describe
  Remy's Connect step instead of exporting tokens.

